2-94e9-53976275dfdd":"meta","01a1b86f-e667-77a3-ad01-c700f43c3e73":"meta","01a1b870-8ceb-7f22-bfaa-6f6a3990b6bf":"meta","01a1b872-aa00-74e0-9980-c3315e23cec4":"meta","01a1b873-da19-7ad0-8627-72b966089007":"meta","01a1b877-9800-7773-af84-51eee275dee9":"meta","01a1b881-c529-7261-b4fb-1b189579af6f":"meta","01a1b883-f1e0-77f3-a79b-d093cf1b8c32":"meta","01a1b884-a0a0-7e90-b960-69a06a57c128":"meta","01a1b887-f5f0-7422-9ffd-4281dbf78bec":"meta","01a1b88a-6cdb-76b1-a9a9-187263327188":"meta","01a1b88a-a39e-7d31-a1e8-35b287ce1da2":"meta","01a1b88c-553b-7690-8d87-ae2c1874ad62":"meta","01a1b88e-7875-7c53-945e-8b326b482140":"meta","01a1b88f-666d-78f2-af8d-00d37a27318d":"meta","01a1b890-afec-7591-b063-9ebe39877502":"meta","01a1b892-0b03-7162-86aa-b454e50bde0a":"meta","01a1b894-5d5d-7541-9811-29fe611f0589":"meta","01a1b895-4e9a-77c0-9ae5-490dcbca553f":"meta","01a1b897-7df6-7751-922c-ba54fdb109c0":"meta","01a1b898-6315-7e90-8ab7-c715f146e5e6":"meta","01a1b89b-0148-7e01-b07f-3eb8b3c0f522":"meta","01a1b89d-f0a0-7e81-b15c-1bbee395b052":"meta","01a1b89e-7cdc-7403-81bc-e3b354fc293c":"meta","01a1b89e-f228-7473-ab72-6e4fd9ff1dc1":"meta","01a1b8a1-8251-7e53-9b07-2136752795f4":"meta","01a1b8a3-6cf8-78e1-bc23-108e190c9dbc":"meta"}},"subagents":{"01a1b7c6-35a1-7711-80f8-b5b2eaee8cb7":{"item":{"agentPath":"main/workflow-agent/1","childSessionId":"89bfa6ff-bbe9-7b63-89b0-135cbb0073cb","controlStatus":"resultReady","depth":1,"durationMs":40119,"fallbackText":"Subagent: Context (verify against workspace docs before assuming): Samsung Galaxy A34 (arm64, Android 16) repurposed as headless Linux server. Termux (F-Droid, com.termux) + Ubuntu 26.04 via proot-distro (no systemd, no Docker, no root). OpenSSH on 8022, key-only auth. supervisord runs Caddy (:8080, basic auth) + filebrowser (:8081) + supervisor UI (:9001). Laptop reaches phone via adb (platform-tools) USB forwards + LAN. Workspace docs: PORTING-NOTES.md, LINUX-SERVER.md, termux-bootstrap.sh, homelab-install.sh, termux-boot-homelab.sh. Owner wants: (a) give Muse Code (Meta harness) access to run on the phone itself, incl. Meta-login auth implications; (b) communicate with the assistant from laptop/phone via chat app, custom web app, or other channels, ideally reusing this homelab.\n\nYOUR SCOPE: running an agentic coding harness (Muse Code / Muse, Meta login) ON the phone itself (Termux/proot Ubuntu). Research: (1) can the Muse Code CLI install and run under proot Ubuntu on arm64 (node/runtime needs, known issues)? (2) how does Meta-login auth work headless (device flow, token storage, expiry, sharing one login across laptop+phone)? (3) resource/feasibility limits (RAM, no systemd, process survival under Android kills) and mitigations reusing the existing tmux+supervisord+Termux:Boot setup. Open the workspace docs listed above and cite them where relevant; use web search for current install/auth docs. Return complete/evidence/unresolved. Every claim needs inspected evidence (file body you opened or a fetched page) or goes in unresolved.","itemId":"fc5dc263-b114-5395-aac0-6c19952c30c8","kind":"subagent","objective":"Context (verify against workspace docs before assuming): Samsung Galaxy A34 (arm64, Android 16) repurposed as headless Linux server. Termux (F-Droid, com.termux) + Ubuntu 26.04 via proot-distro (no systemd, no Docker, no root). OpenSSH on 8022, key-only auth. supervisord runs Caddy (:8080, basic auth) + filebrowser (:8081) + supervisor UI (:9001). Laptop reaches phone via adb (platform-tools) USB forwards + LAN. Workspace docs: PORTING-NOTES.md, LINUX-SERVER.md, termux-bootstrap.sh, homelab-install.sh, termux-boot-homelab.sh. Owner wants: (a) give Muse Code (Meta harness) access to run on the phone itself, incl. Meta-login auth implications; (b) communicate with the assistant from laptop/phone via chat app, custom web app, or other channels, ideally reusing this homelab.\n\nYOUR SCOPE: running an agentic coding harness (Muse Code / Muse, Meta login) ON the phone itself (Termux/proot Ubuntu). Research: (1) can the Muse Code CLI install and run under proot Ubuntu on arm64 (node/runtime needs, known issues)? (2) how does Meta-login auth work headless (device flow, token storage, expiry, sharing one login across laptop+phone)? (3) resource/feasibility limits (RAM, no systemd, process survival under Android kills) and mitigations reusing the existing tmux+supervisord+Termux:Boot setup. Open the workspace docs listed above and cite them where relevant; use web search for current install/auth docs. Return complete/evidence/unresolved. Every claim needs inspected evidence (file body you opened or a fetched page) or goes in unresolved.","recordedAt":"2026-11-07T20:50:23.46034Z","result":{"artifactRefs":[],"evidenceRefs":["run://991873a2-2be9-7b63-8894-247e04d5a517","\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\.local\\share\\muse\\sessions\\2026\\11\\07\\01a1b712-7955-7a03-a1d7-21c1c82d4320\\session.jsonl"],"structuredData":{"complete":true,"evidence":["Workspace LINUX-SERVER.md inspected: A34 SM-A346B arm64, 7.4G RAM, Ubuntu 26.04 via proot-distro, no systemd/no Docker, supervisord->Caddy :8080->filebrowser :8081 + supervisor UI :9001, tmux session homelab + 5-min curl watchdog, Termux:Boot autostart proven after reboot, phone-side curl -o broken under proot so binaries adb-pushed from laptop, daemonized supervisord SIGKILLED under screen-off (foreground -n in tmux survives).","Install: muse CLI is statically linked, needs only curl+mktemp+bash, no Node/Python; Linux x86_64+arm64 supported incl. Ubuntu 20.04+; one-liner curl -fsSL https://dev.meta.ai/install.sh | bash; launcher at ~/.local/bin/muse + muse-bin-<version>; Linux arm64 binary ~213 MiB (sources: codersera install guide, backgrind, jacar.es, toolian docs via web search). Ubuntu 26.04 arm64 under proot satisfies glibc arm64 requirement in principle; proot syscall/ptrace overhead ~40-50% UNIXbench penalty, worst for syscall/IO-heavy work (sources: kern runtime-exec research, ggprompts/termux guide via search). Caveat: proot mishandles getifaddrs()/os.networkInterfaces for Node apps and phone-side curl -o fails (workspace doc) -- same class of risk applies to the muse self-updating launcher until tested on-device.","Auth headless: muse login is OAuth2 device-code flow (prints code + verification URL, approve in browser) and works fine over SSH with no local browser; non-interactive/CI route is a Model API key via META_API_KEY env or muse auth set --api-key-stdin; credentials cache locally so no re-auth per session; META_API_KEY wins over logged-in session (sources: codersera guide, musecodes.io docs, qainsights, aq.dev VPS guide via search/fetch). Implication: do the device-flow login once over SSH (phone needs outbound HTTPS only), or drop an API key for unattended runs; sharing one personal login across laptop+phone concurrency/expiry not verified -- in unresolved.","Feasibility/mitigation reusing existing setup: run muse/muse exec inside proot Ubuntu under the existing tmux+supervisord pattern (new supervisor program or second tmux session), keep Termux battery-whitelist + Termux:Boot + watchdog; expect ~200+MB binary + model-context RAM pressure on 6-7.4GB device -- keep sessions headless (muse exec), one at a time; updater hourly self-update can be pinned with MUSE_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1; filebrowser-archived warning in workspace doc irrelevant to this task."],"unresolved":["Exact on-disk token/keychain path and refresh-token expiry for muse login (only summarized as 'credentials cache locally' -- underlying file not inspected; needs muse login --help / docs page on dev.meta.ai).","Whether one Meta login can be concurrently active on laptop + phone, or forces logout/session conflict (no inspected evidence).","On-device proof: muse installer launcher platform-detection + binary execution under proot on this specific phone untested (proot getifaddrs/curl -o class issues suggest testing download + first run on-device before relying on it)."]},"summary":"structured result submitted"},"revision":5,"role":"workflow-agent","status":"inProgress","subagentId":"01a1b7c6-35a1-7711-80f8-b5b2eaee8cb7","turnId":"01a1b7c5-a944-7f03-b294-f5c3e0964d0e","usage":{"cacheReadTokens":107844,"cacheWriteTokens":0,"cachedTokens":107844,"inputTokens":143377,"outputTokens":1787,"reasoningTokens":239},"workflowRunId":"workflow-run-model-tool-call_01a1b7c610df7134a294d7c0e84a6431"},"opened_ordinal":1560,"span":{"first":{"id":"01a1b712-7955-726e-9493-94e41249c95d","sequence":8690},"last":{"id":"01a1b7c6-d464-7d92-9768-bc61da9ab028","sequence":8725},"stream_id":"01a1b712-7955-7a03-a1d7-21c1c82d4320","stream_kind":"session"}},"01a1b7c6-3637-7063-a0b8-b2807d214a54":{"item":{"agentPath":"main/workflow-agent/2","childSessionId":"89bfa7ff-bbe9-7d16-89b0-145cbb00757e","controlStatus":"resultReady","depth":1,"durationMs":38800,"fallbackText":"Subagent: Context (verify against workspace docs before assuming): Samsung Galaxy A34 (arm64, Android 16) repurposed as headless Linux server. Termux (F-Droid, com.termux) + Ubuntu 26.04 via proot-distro (no systemd, no Docker, no root). OpenSSH on 8022, key-only auth. supervisord runs Caddy (:8080, basic auth) + filebrowser (:8081) + supervisor UI (:9001). Laptop reaches phone via adb (platform-tools) USB forwards + LAN. Workspace docs: PORTING-NOTES.md, LINUX-SERVER.md, termux-bootstrap.sh, homelab-install.sh, termux-boot-homelab.sh. Owner wants: (a) give Muse Code (Meta harness) access to run on the phone itself, incl. Meta-login auth implications; (b) communicate with the assistant from laptop/phone via chat app, custom web app, or other channels, ideally reusing this homelab.\n\nYOUR SCOPE: communication channels between the owner (laptop and/or phone) and an assistant/agent running on the phone. Research and compare: (1) chat apps with bot APIs usable from the phone side (e.g. Telegram bot via plain HTTPS polling — no inbound ports, works behind NAT); (2) a custom minimal web chat app served through the existing Caddy front door (auth, websockets/SSE under proot, arm64 static binaries); (3) plain SSH + tmux sharing from laptop/phone (Termux, Blink, Tailscale/Cloudflare options for off-LAN). For each: what runs where, auth story, what breaks on reboot/Doze, and fit with the existing Caddy-basic-auth + no-public-internet posture. Open the workspace docs; use web search for current facts. Return complete/evidence/unresolved. Every claim needs inspected evidence or goes in unresolved.","itemId":"9c43270d-8e26-55bf-831d-1d560147ea07","kind":"subagent","objective":"Context (verify against workspace docs before assuming): Samsung Galaxy A34 (arm64, Android 16) repurposed as headless Linux server. Termux (F-Droid, com.termux) + Ubuntu 26.04 via proot-distro (no systemd, no Docker, no root). OpenSSH on 8022, key-only auth. supervisord runs Caddy (:8080, basic auth) + filebrowser (:8081) + supervisor UI (:9001). Laptop reaches phone via adb (platform-tools) USB forwards + LAN. Workspace docs: PORTING-NOTES.md, LINUX-SERVER.md, termux-bootstrap.sh, homelab-install.sh, termux-boot-homelab.sh. Owner wants: (a) give Muse Code (Meta harness) access to run on the phone itself, incl. Meta-login auth implications; (b) communicate with the assistant from laptop/phone via chat app, custom web app, or other channels, ideally reusing this homelab.\n\nYOUR SCOPE: communication channels between the owner (laptop and/or phone) and an assistant/agent running on the phone. Research and compare: (1) chat apps with bot APIs usable from the phone side (e.g. Telegram bot via plain HTTPS polling — no inbound ports, works behind NAT); (2) a custom minimal web chat app served through the existing Caddy front door (auth, websockets/SSE under proot, arm64 static binaries); (3) plain SSH + tmux sharing from laptop/phone (Termux, Blink, Tailscale/Cloudflare options for off-LAN). For each: what runs where, auth story, what breaks on reboot/Doze, and fit with the existing Caddy-basic-auth + no-public-internet posture. Open the workspace docs; use web search for current facts. Return complete/evidence/unresolved. Every claim needs inspected evidence or goes in unresolved.","recordedAt":"2026-11-07T20:50:22.407502Z","result":{"artifactRefs":[],"evidenceRefs":["run://991874a2-2be9-7d16-8894-257e04d5a6ca","\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\.local\\share\\muse\\sessions\\2026\\11\\07\\01a1b712-7955-7a03-a1d7-21c1c82d4320\\session.jsonl"],"structuredData":{"complete":true,"evidence":["Workspace LINUX-SERVER.md inspected: A34 arm64/Android16, Termux F-Droid + proot Ubuntu 26.04 (no systemd/Docker), sshd:8022 key-only, supervisord->Caddy:8080 basic-auth front + filebrowser:8081 + supervisor UI:9001; adb forwards wiped on reboot, sshd does not autostart without Termux:Boot; daemonized supervisord SIGKILLed under screen-off -> runs foreground -n in tmux 'homelab' via ~/.termux/boot/homelab.sh + 5-min curl watchdog; battery whitelist + never-sleeping apps + charger required; filebrowser v2 archived 2026-09-01 keep only behind Caddy auth.","homelab-install.sh inspected: Caddy arm64 tgz + filebrowser arm64 tgz adb-pushed (phone-side curl -o broken, error 23); Caddyfile :8080 basic_auth + reverse_proxy to :8081 and :9001, auto_https/admin off; supervisord uses 'port=127.0.0.1:9001' (http_port invalid) with supervisorctl serverurl http://127.0.0.1:9001 (unix socket missing under proot).","termux-boot-homelab.sh inspected: boot script runs sshd + tmux new -d -s homelab 'proot-distro login ubuntu -- supervisord -n' + background 300s watchdog restarting session unless :8080 returns 401.","termux-bootstrap.sh inspected: pkg openssh/proot-distro/termux-api, passwd+sshd, proot Ubuntu + tmux; hardening note in LINUX-SERVER.md: do NOT expose SSH directly, use Tailscale/WireGuard; keep adb authorized to laptop only.","Option1 Telegram bot (web sources 2026): BotFather token; getUpdates long-polling = outbound HTTPS only, no public IP/ports/certs, works behind NAT/firewall; single consumer per token; polling and webhook mutually exclusive; webhook would need ports 443/80/88/8443+TLS (not usable here). Fit: best off-LAN channel preserving no-public-internet posture; runs as python script under proot/tmux or supervisord; secret = bot token + allowlist chat-id; risk: depends on api.telegram.org reachability + token hygiene; Doze/phantom-killer applies equally (needs whitelist/wakelock/boot like other services).","Option2 custom web chat via Caddy (web sources): Caddy reverse_proxy passes Upgrade/websocket with no extra directives and streams SSE; single static arm64 binary (already proven pattern in repo). Fit: runs where filebrowser runs (extra supervisord program, e.g. :8082, Caddy handle /chat/* + basic_auth or token); reachable on LAN via adb forward tcp:8080 or phone LAN IP:8080; off-LAN only via Tailscale/tunnel, never port-forward; reboot/Doze same as existing stack (Termux:Boot tmux + watchdog covers it). Cost: must build auth/session/agent-bridge yourself; keep filebrowser archived-binary risk in mind (upstream archived 2026-09-01, no fixes; Quantum/copyparty are maintained successors).","Option3 SSH+tmux (workspace + web sources): already proven (key-only :8022, tmux installed by bootstrap, homelab already in tmux). Laptop: ssh -p 8022 over adb forward or LAN; phone-local: Termux terminal. Off-LAN: Tailscale/Headscale WireGuard mesh gives stable 100.x IPs, no port forwarding, works behind NAT/CGNAT with DERP fallback; Tailscale SSH optional. Reboot: adb forwards wiped (re-add), sshd needs Termux:Boot autostart; Doze/phantom-process killer (Android 12+) kills background sshd/services unless Termux+Boot exempted (Unrestricted), wake-lock, charger; vendor autostart toggles per dontkillmyapp. Blink/mosh notes: Blink is iOS-only so irrelevant to A34+laptop; mosh needs UDP and is optional."],"unresolved":["No inspected evidence of outbound internet reachability from the phone (api.telegram.org, Tailscale DERP) — assumed available; verify with curl from Termux/proot before committing to Telegram or Tailscale.","Whether owner will install Tailscale app/Headscale vs staying LAN+adb-only — decision needed; no-public-internet posture favors Tailscale tailnet over any port-forward.","Exact agent runtime on phone (part a, out of scope) not inspected — chat-channel choice only defines transport; the agent-to-chat bridge process still needs specifying."]},"summary":"structured result submitted"},"revision":5,"role":"workflow-agent","status":"inProgress","subagentId":"01a1b7c6-3637-7063-a0b8-b2807d214a54","turnId":"01a1b7c5-a944-7f03-b294-f5c3e0964d0e","usage":{"cacheReadTokens":111172,"cacheWriteTokens":0,"cachedTokens":111172,"inputTokens":148529,"outputTokens":2220,"reasoningTokens":153},"workflowRunId":"workflow-run-model-tool-call_01a1b7c610df7134a294d7c0e84a6431"},"opened_ordinal":1566,"span":{"first":{"id":"01a1b712-7955-7070-b2ba-3df21cc7a2df","sequence":8704},"last":{"id":"01a1b7c6-d047-77f0-afc1-974ee9a588f2","sequence":8718},"stream_id":"01a1b712-7955-7a03-a1d7-21c1c82d4320","stream_kind":"session"}},"01a1b7c6-d548-71c1-92e4-ff87fb0e89cf":{"item":{"agentPath":"main/workflow-agent/3","childSessionId":"91643929-6e9a-79c7-858f-b37f74207f7f","controlStatus":"resultReady","depth":1,"durationMs":15380,"fallbackText":"Subagent: Workflow result handoff sha256:71ad38e9d8ffa25d37e3daf2617ad720cd5e07748a7cf461fec2e744d806c433\nCaller input bytes=7729:\nFind concrete gaps, contradictions, or unverified claims in this compact evidence (missing auth details, untested install paths, single-source claims): [{\"scope\":\"primary-0\",\"ref\":\"prior result 2\",\"complete\":false,\"evidence\":[\"Workspace LINUX-SERVER.md inspected: A34 SM-A346B arm64, 7.4G RAM, Ubuntu 26.04 via proot-distro, no systemd/no Docker, supervisord->Caddy :8080->filebrowser :8081 + supervisor UI :9001, tmux session homelab + 5-min curl watchdog, Termux:Boot autostart proven after reboot, phone-side curl -o broken under proot so binaries adb-pushed from laptop, daemonized supervisord SIGKILLED under screen-off (foreground -n in tmux survives).\",\"Install: muse CLI is statically linked, needs only curl+mktemp+bash, no Node/Python; Linux x86_64+arm64 supported incl. Ubuntu 20.04+; one-liner curl -fsSL https://dev.meta.ai/install.sh | bash; launcher at ~/.local/bin/muse + muse-bin-<version>; Linux arm64 binary ~213 MiB (sources: codersera install guide, backgrind, jacar.es, toolian docs via web search). Ubuntu 26.04 arm64 under proot satisfies glibc arm64 requirement in principle; proot syscall/ptrace overhead ~40-50% UNIXbench penalty, worst for syscall/IO-heavy work (sources: kern runtime-exec research, ggprompts/termux guide via search). Caveat: proot mishandles getifaddrs()/os.networkInterfaces for Node apps and phone-side curl -o fails (workspace doc) -- same class of risk applies to the muse self-updating launcher until tested on-device.\",\"Auth headless: muse login is OAuth2 device-code flow (prints code + verification URL, approve in browser) and works fine over SSH with no local browser; non-interactive/CI route is a Model API key via META_API_KEY env or muse auth set --api-key-stdin; credentials cache locally so no re-auth per session; META_API_KEY wins over logged-in session (sources: codersera guide, musecodes.io docs, qainsights, aq.dev VPS guide via search/fetch). Implication: do the device-flow login once over SSH (phone needs outbound HTTPS only), or drop an API key for unattended runs; sharing one personal login across laptop+phone concurrency/expiry not verified -- in unresolved.\",\"Feasibility/mitigation reusing existing setup: run muse/muse exec inside proot Ubuntu under the existing tmux+supervisord pattern (new supervisor program or second tmux session), keep Termux battery-whitelist + Termux:Boot + watchdog; expect ~200+MB binary + model-context RAM pressure on 6-7.4GB device -- keep sessions headless (muse exec), one at a time; updater hourly self-update can be pinned with MUSE_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1; filebrowser-archived warning in workspace doc irrelevant to this task.\"],\"notes\":[],\"unresolved\":[\"Exact on-disk token/keychain path and refresh-token expiry for muse login (only summarized as 'credentials cache locally' -- underlying file not inspected; needs muse login --help / docs page on dev.meta.ai).\",\"Whether one Meta login can be concurrently active on laptop + phone, or forces logout/session conflict (no inspected evidence).\",\"On-device proof: muse installer launcher platform-detection + binary execution under proot on this specific phone untested (proot getifaddrs/curl -o class issues suggest testing download + first run on-device before relying on it).\"]},{\"scope\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"complete\":false,\"evidence\":[\"Workspace LINUX-SERVER.md inspected: A34 arm64/Android16, Termux F-Droid + proot Ubuntu 26.04 (no systemd/Docker), sshd:8022 key-only, supervisord->Caddy:8080 basic-auth front + filebrowser:8081 + supervisor UI:9001; adb forwards wiped on reboot, sshd does not autostart without Termux:Boot; daemonized supervisord SIGKILLed under screen-off -> runs foreground -n in tmux 'homelab' via ~/.termux/boot/homelab.sh + 5-min curl watchdog; battery whitelist + never-sleeping apps + charger required; filebrowser v2 archived 2026-09-01 keep only behind Caddy auth.\",\"homelab-install.sh inspected: Caddy arm64 tgz + filebrowser arm64 tgz adb-pushed (phone-side curl -o broken, error 23); Caddyfile :8080 basic_auth + reverse_proxy to :8081 and :9001, auto_https/admin off; supervisord uses 'port=127.0.0.1:9001' (http_port invalid) with supervisorctl serverurl http://127.0.0.1:9001 (unix socket missing under proot).\",\"termux-boot-homelab.sh inspected: boot script runs sshd + tmux new -d -s homelab 'proot-distro login ubuntu -- supervisord -n' + background 300s watchdog restarting session unless :8080 returns 401.\",\"termux-bootstrap.sh inspected: pkg openssh/proot-distro/termux-api, passwd+sshd, proot Ubuntu + tmux; hardening note in LINUX-SERVER.md: do NOT expose SSH directly, use Tailscale/WireGuard; keep adb authorized to laptop only.\",\"Option1 Telegram bot (web sources 2026): BotFather token; getUpdates long-polling = outbound HTTPS only, no public IP/ports/certs, works behind NAT/firewall; single consumer per token; polling and webhook mutually exclusive; webhook would need ports 443/80/88/8443+TLS (not usable here). Fit: best off-LAN channel preserving no-public-internet posture; runs as python script under proot/tmux or supervisord; secret = bot token + allowlist chat-id; risk: depends on api.telegram.org reachability + token hygiene; Doze/phantom-killer applies equally (needs whitelist/wakelock/boot like other services).\",\"Option2 custom web chat via Caddy (web sources): Caddy reverse_proxy passes Upgrade/websocket with no extra directives and streams SSE; single static arm64 binary (already proven pattern in repo). Fit: runs where filebrowser runs (extra supervisord program, e.g. :8082, Caddy handle /chat/* + basic_auth or token); reachable on LAN via adb forward tcp:8080 or phone LAN IP:8080; off-LAN only via Tailscale/tunnel, never port-forward; reboot/Doze same as existing stack (Termux:Boot tmux + watchdog covers it). Cost: must build auth/session/agent-bridge yourself; keep filebrowser archived-binary risk in mind (upstream archived 2026-09-01, no fixes; Quantum/copyparty are maintained successors).\",\"Option3 SSH+tmux (workspace + web sources): already proven (key-only :8022, tmux installed by bootstrap, homelab already in tmux). Laptop: ssh -p 8022 over adb forward or LAN; phone-local: Termux terminal. Off-LAN: Tailscale/Headscale WireGuard mesh gives stable 100.x IPs, no port forwarding, works behind NAT/CGNAT with DERP fallback; Tailscale SSH optional. Reboot: adb forwards wiped (re-add), sshd needs Termux:Boot autostart; Doze/phantom-process killer (Android 12+) kills background sshd/services unless Termux+Boot exempted (Unrestricted), wake-lock, charger; vendor autostart toggles per dontkillmyapp. Blink/mosh notes: Blink is iOS-only so irrelevant to A34+laptop; mosh needs UDP and is optional.\"],\"notes\":[{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"Recommendation: Telegram long-polling bot for off-LAN async control (zero inbound, keeps no-public-internet posture) + keep Caddy basic-auth web UI for LAN-rich sessions + SSH+tmux over Tailscale for full terminal; all three share the existing Termux:Boot tmux + watchdog persistence. Never expose :8022/:8080/:8081 directly; rotate the admin password noted OPEN in LINUX-SERVER.md.\"}],\"unresolved\":[\"No inspected evidence of outbound internet reachability from the phone (api.telegram.org, Tailscale DERP) — assumed available; verify with curl from Termux/proot before committing to Telegram or Tailscale.\",\"Whether owner will install Tailscale app/Headscale vs staying LAN+adb-only — decision needed; no-public-internet posture favors Tailscale tailnet over any port-forward.\",\"Exact agent runtime on phone (part a, out of scope) not inspected — chat-channel choice only defines transport; the agent-to-chat bridge process still needs specifying.\"]}]. Return complete/evidence/unresolved.\nPrior result index:\nRead the complete prior result index with read_file using {\"path\":\"\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\danie\\\\.local\\\\share\\\\muse\\\\sessions\\\\2026\\\\11\\\\07\\\\01a1b712-7955-7a03-a1d7-21c1c82d4320\\\\tool-outputs\\\\workflow-results\\\\handoff-b61b8ba97aa01b075147f5be9f72d6d54970b23212021addcf9b04afadb7bd25-883df04199edae552788772ebc2d098ba59f575cfde0fd1c925082acd23b8571.txt\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":500}; keep limit at 500 and increment offset by 500 while the output says \"(more lines below)\". If a part cannot be read, name that gap and use the other readable evidence.","itemId":"2a6d8a82-c189-55aa-a505-f7c42b29360c","kind":"subagent","objective":"Workflow result handoff sha256:71ad38e9d8ffa25d37e3daf2617ad720cd5e07748a7cf461fec2e744d806c433\nCaller input bytes=7729:\nFind conc