side curl -o broken, error 23); Caddyfile :8080 basic_auth + reverse_proxy to :8081 and :9001, auto_https/admin off; supervisord uses 'port=127.0.0.1:9001' (http_port invalid) with supervisorctl serverurl http://127.0.0.1:9001 (unix socket missing under proot).\",\"termux-boot-homelab.sh inspected: boot script runs sshd + tmux new -d -s homelab 'proot-distro login ubuntu -- supervisord -n' + background 300s watchdog restarting session unless :8080 returns 401.\",\"termux-bootstrap.sh inspected: pkg openssh/proot-distro/termux-api, passwd+sshd, proot Ubuntu + tmux; hardening note in LINUX-SERVER.md: do NOT expose SSH directly, use Tailscale/WireGuard; keep adb authorized to laptop only.\",\"Option1 Telegram bot (web sources 2026): BotFather token; getUpdates long-polling = outbound HTTPS only, no public IP/ports/certs, works behind NAT/firewall; single consumer per token; polling and webhook mutually exclusive; webhook would need ports 443/80/88/8443+TLS (not usable here). Fit: best off-LAN channel preserving no-public-internet posture; runs as python script under proot/tmux or supervisord; secret = bot token + allowlist chat-id; risk: depends on api.telegram.org reachability + token hygiene; Doze/phantom-killer applies equally (needs whitelist/wakelock/boot like other services).\",\"Option2 custom web chat via Caddy (web sources): Caddy reverse_proxy passes Upgrade/websocket with no extra directives and streams SSE; single static arm64 binary (already proven pattern in repo). Fit: runs where filebrowser runs (extra supervisord program, e.g. :8082, Caddy handle /chat/* + basic_auth or token); reachable on LAN via adb forward tcp:8080 or phone LAN IP:8080; off-LAN only via Tailscale/tunnel, never port-forward; reboot/Doze same as existing stack (Termux:Boot tmux + watchdog covers it). Cost: must build auth/session/agent-bridge yourself; keep filebrowser archived-binary risk in mind (upstream archived 2026-09-01, no fixes; Quantum/copyparty are maintained successors).\",\"Option3 SSH+tmux (workspace + web sources): already proven (key-only :8022, tmux installed by bootstrap, homelab already in tmux). Laptop: ssh -p 8022 over adb forward or LAN; phone-local: Termux terminal. Off-LAN: Tailscale/Headscale WireGuard mesh gives stable 100.x IPs, no port forwarding, works behind NAT/CGNAT with DERP fallback; Tailscale SSH optional. Reboot: adb forwards wiped (re-add), sshd needs Termux:Boot autostart; Doze/phantom-process killer (Android 12+) kills background sshd/services unless Termux+Boot exempted (Unrestricted), wake-lock, charger; vendor autostart toggles per dontkillmyapp. Blink/mosh notes: Blink is iOS-only so irrelevant to A34+laptop; mosh needs UDP and is optional.\"],\"notes\":[{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"Recommendation: Telegram long-polling bot for off-LAN async control (zero inbound, keeps no-public-internet posture) + keep Caddy basic-auth web UI for LAN-rich sessions + SSH+tmux over Tailscale for full terminal; all three share the existing Termux:Boot tmux + watchdog persistence. Never expose :8022/:8080/:8081 directly; rotate the admin password noted OPEN in LINUX-SERVER.md.\"}],\"unresolved\":[\"No inspected evidence of outbound internet reachability from the phone (api.telegram.org, Tailscale DERP) — assumed available; verify with curl from Termux/proot before committing to Telegram or Tailscale.\",\"Whether owner will install Tailscale app/Headscale vs staying LAN+adb-only — decision needed; no-public-internet posture favors Tailscale tailnet over any port-forward.\",\"Exact agent runtime on phone (part a, out of scope) not inspected — chat-channel choice only defines transport; the agent-to-chat bridge process still needs specifying.\"]}]. Return complete/evidence/unresolved.\nPrior result index:\nRead the complete prior result index with read_file using {\"path\":\"\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\danie\\\\.local\\\\share\\\\muse\\\\sessions\\\\2026\\\\11\\\\07\\\\01a1b712-7955-7a03-