ion (10 hits, multi-source not single-source): install one-liner curl -fsSL https://dev.meta.ai/install.sh | bash, ~/.local/bin/muse launcher, Linux x86_64+arm64 incl. Ubuntu, needs only bash+curl; auth META_API_KEY env wins > stored key > browser session, muse auth set --api-key-stdin, keys LLM_-prefixed, device/browser OAuth over SSH. Downgrades 'single-source' risk for install/auth commands.","Remaining unverified: muse launcher platform-detect + exec under proot on this phone untested (same curl -o/download class failure documented); exact on-disk token path + refresh expiry uninspected; concurrent laptop+phone single-login conflict untested; phone outbound reachability to api.telegram.org / Tailscale DERP / dev.meta.ai never curled from Termux/proot; Caddy websocket/SSE passthrough and /chat route not in repo Caddyfile (unbuilt); watchdog Termux-localhost vs proot-localhost equivalence assumed from passing curls but fragile."],"unresolved":["Termux-side tmux+curl provenance: bootstrap does not pkg-install them; verify on-device or amend bootstrap.","RAM contradiction 6GB vs 7.4G: resolve before sizing muse sessions.","On-device proof: muse installer download + first run under proot; phone outbound HTTPS (dev.meta.ai, api.telegram.org, Tailscale DERP).","Exact muse credential path/expiry and concurrent-login behavior.","Owner decision: Tailscale vs LAN+adb-only; admin password rotation still OPEN."]},"summary":"structured result submitted"},"revision":5,"role":"workflow-agent","status":"inProgress","subagentId":"01a1b7c6-d548-71c1-92e4-ff87fb0e89cf","turnId":"01a1b7c5-a944-7f03-b294-f5c3e0964d0e","usage":{"cacheReadTokens":113604,"cacheWriteTokens":0,"cachedTokens":113604,"inputTokens":149819,"outputTokens":2346,"reasoningTokens":736},"workflowRunId":"workflow-run-model-tool-call_01a1b7c610df7134a294d7c0e84a6431"},"opened_ordinal":1582,"span":{"first":{"id":"01a1b712-7955-70de-ac7a-e737bffba8f7","sequence":8732},"last":{"id":"01a1b7c7-12c5-7422-9dbc-9a0d0dd898ed","sequence":8746},"stream_id":"01a1b712-7955-7a03-a1d7-21c1c82d4320","stream_kind":"session"}},"01a1b7c7-13e6-7f90-a74d-ff7246dbbafd":{"item":{"agentPath":"main/workflow-agent/4","childSessionId":"91643629-6e9a-74ae-858f-b07f74207a66","controlStatus":"resultReady","depth":1,"durationMs":32864,"fallbackText":"Subagent: Workflow result handoff sha256:47057aa247e2f32dbeb0489874af9d41c8a41b397cdce8a88ab2ccfc890d04c2\nCaller input bytes=10685:\nResolve this exact gap once with fresh inspection (workspace files and/or web fetch), or return it unchanged: {\"gap\":\"Exact on-disk token/keychain path and refresh-token expiry for muse login (only summarized as 'credentials cache locally' -- underlying file not inspected; needs muse login --help / docs page on dev.meta.ai).\",\"reports\":[{\"scope\":\"primary-0\",\"ref\":\"prior result 2\",\"complete\":false,\"evidence\":[\"Workspace LINUX-SERVER.md inspected: A34 SM-A346B arm64, 7.4G RAM, Ubuntu 26.04 via proot-distro, no systemd/no Docker, supervisord->Caddy :8080->filebrowser :8081 + supervisor UI :9001, tmux session homelab + 5-min curl watchdog, Termux:Boot autostart proven after reboot, phone-side curl -o broken under proot so binaries adb-pushed from laptop, daemonized supervisord SIGKILLED under screen-off (foreground -n in tmux survives).\",\"Install: muse CLI is statically linked, needs only curl+mktemp+bash, no Node/Python; Linux x86_64+arm64 supported incl. Ubuntu 20.04+; one-liner curl -fsSL https://dev.meta.ai/install.sh | bash; launcher at ~/.local/bin/muse + muse-bin-<version>; Linux arm64 binary ~213 MiB (sources: codersera install guide, backgrind, jacar.es, toolian docs via web search). Ubuntu 26.04 arm64 under proot satisfies glibc arm64 requirement in principle; proot syscall/ptrace overhead ~40-50% UNIXbench penalty, worst for syscall/IO-heavy work (sources: kern runtime-exec research, ggprompts/termux guide via search). Caveat: proot mishandles getifaddrs()/os.networkInterfaces for Node apps and phone-side curl -o fails (workspace doc) -- same class of risk applies to the muse self-updating launcher until tested on-device.\",\"Auth headless: muse login is OAuth2 device-code flow (prints code + verification URL, approve in browser) and works fine over SSH with no local browser; non-interactive/CI route is a Model API key via META_API_KEY env or muse auth set --api-key-stdin; credentials cache locally so no re-auth per session; META_API_KEY wins over logged-in session (sources: codersera guide, musecodes.io docs, qainsights, aq.dev VPS guide via search/fetch). Implication: do the device-flow login once over SSH (phone needs outbound HTTPS only), or drop an API key for unattended runs; sharing one personal login across laptop+phone concurrency/expiry not verified -- in unresolved.\",\"Feasibility/mitigation reusing existing setup: run muse/muse exec inside proot Ubuntu under the existing tmux+supervisord pattern (new supervisor program or second tmux session), keep Termux battery-whitelist + Termux:Boot + watchdog; expect ~200+MB binary + model-context RAM pressure on 6-7.4GB device -- keep sessions headless (muse exec), one at a time; updater hourly self-update can be pinned with MUSE_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1; filebrowser-archived warning in workspace doc irrelevant to this task.\"],\"notes\":[],\"unresolved\":[\"Exact on-disk token/keychain path and refresh-token expiry for muse login (only summarized as 'credentials cache locally' -- underlying file not inspected; needs muse login --help / docs page on dev.meta.ai).\",\"Whether one Meta login can be concurrently active on laptop + phone, or forces logout/session conflict (no inspected evidence).\",\"On-device proof: muse installer launcher platform-detection + binary execution under proot on this specific phone untested (proot getifaddrs/curl -o class issues suggest testing download + first run on-device before relying on it).\"]},{\"scope\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"complete\":false,\"evidence\":[\"Workspace LINUX-SERVER.md inspected: A34 arm64/Android16, Termux F-Droid + proot Ubuntu 26.04 (no systemd/Docker), sshd:8022 key-only, supervisord->Caddy:8080 basic-auth front + filebrowser:8081 + supervisor UI:9001; adb forwards wiped on reboot, sshd does not autostart without Termux:Boot; daemonized supervisord SIGKILLed under screen-off -> runs foreground -n in tmux 'homelab' via ~/.termux/boot/homelab.sh + 5-min curl watchdog; battery whitelist + never-sleeping apps + charger required; filebrowser v2 archived 2026-09-01 keep only behind Caddy auth.\",\"homelab-install.sh inspected: Caddy arm64 tgz + filebrowser arm64 tgz adb-pushed (phone-side curl -o broken, error 23); Caddyfile :8080 basic_auth + reverse_proxy to :8081 and :9001, auto_https/admin off; supervisord uses 'port=127.0.0.1:9001' (http_port invalid) with supervisorctl serverurl http://127.0.0.1:9001 (unix socket missing under proot).\",\"termux-boot-homelab.sh inspected: boot script runs sshd + tmux new -d -s homelab 'proot-distro login ubuntu -- supervisord -n' + background 300s watchdog restarting session unless :8080 returns 401.\",\"termux-bootstrap.sh inspected: pkg openssh/proot-distro/termux-api, passwd+sshd, proot Ubuntu + tmux; hardening note in LINUX-SERVER.md: do NOT expose SSH directly, use Tailscale/WireGuard; keep adb authorized to laptop only.\",\"Option1 Telegram bot (web sources 2026): BotFather token; getUpdates long-polling = outbound HTTPS only, no public IP/ports/certs, works behind NAT/firewall; single consumer per token; polling and webhook mutually exclusive; webhook would need ports 443/80/88/8443+TLS (not usable here). Fit: best off-LAN channel preserving no-public-internet posture; runs as python script under proot/tmux or supervisord; secret = bot token + allowlist chat-id; risk: depends on api.telegram.org reachability + token hygiene; Doze/phantom-killer applies equally (needs whitelist/wakelock/boot like other services).\",\"Option2 custom web chat via Caddy (web sources): Caddy reverse_proxy passes Upgrade/websocket with no extra directives and streams SSE; single static arm64 binary (already proven pattern in repo). Fit: runs where filebrowser runs (extra supervisord program, e.g. :8082, Caddy handle /chat/* + basic_auth or token); reachable on LAN via adb forward tcp:8080 or phone LAN IP:8080; off-LAN only via Tailscale/tunnel, never port-forward; reboot/Doze same as existing stack (Termux:Boot tmux + watchdog covers it). Cost: must build auth/session/agent-bridge yourself; keep filebrowser archived-binary risk in mind (upstream archived 2026-09-01, no fixes; Quantum/copyparty are maintained successors).\",\"Option3 SSH+tmux (workspace + web sources): already proven (key-only :8022, tmux installed by bootstrap, homelab already in tmux). Laptop: ssh -p 8022 over adb forward or LAN; phone-local: Termux terminal. Off-LAN: Tailscale/Headscale WireGuard mesh gives stable 100.x IPs, no port forwarding, works behind NAT/CGNAT with DERP fallback; Tailscale SSH optional. Reboot: adb forwards wiped (re-add), sshd needs Termux:Boot autostart; Doze/phantom-process killer (Android 12+) kills background sshd/services unless Termux+Boot exempted (Unrestricted), wake-lock, charger; vendor autostart toggles per dontkillmyapp. Blink/mosh notes: Blink is iOS-only so irrelevant to A34+laptop; mosh needs UDP and is optional.\"],\"notes\":[{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"Recommendation: Telegram long-polling bot for off-LAN async control (zero inbound, keeps no-public-internet posture) + keep Caddy basic-auth web UI for LAN-rich sessions + SSH+tmux over Tailscale for full terminal; all three share the existing Termux:Boot tmux + watchdog persistence. Never expose :8022/:8080/:8081 directly; rotate the admin password noted OPEN in LINUX-SERVER.md.\"}],\"unresolved\":[\"No inspected evidence of outbound internet reachability from the phone (api.telegram.org, Tailscale DERP) — assumed available; verify with curl from Termux/proot before committing to Telegram or Tailscale.\",\"Whether owner will install Tailscale app/Headscale vs staying LAN+adb-only — decision needed; no-public-internet posture favors Tailscale tailnet over any port-forward.\",\"Exact agent runtime on phone (part a, out of scope) not inspected — chat-channel choice only defines transport; the agent-to-chat bridge process still needs specifying.\"]},{\"scope\":\"critic\",\"ref\":\"prior result 3\",\"complete\":false,\"evidence\":[\"Inspected LINUX-SERVER.md: SM-A346B arm64, 7.4G RAM, Ubuntu 26.04 proot, no systemd/Docker, supervisord->Caddy :8080->filebrowser :8081 + :9001, foreground -n in tmux homelab + 300s watchdog, phone-side curl -o error 23 -> adb-push binaries, daemonized supervisord SIGKILLed screen-off, Termux:Boot proven after reboot, OPEN admin-password rotation, filebrowser v2 archived 2026-09-01.\",\"Inspected homelab-install.sh: guards ~/caddy.tgz ~/fb.tgz adb-push, Caddyfile :8080 basic_auth + /supervisor/* -> :9001 + /* -> :8081 with admin off/auto_https off, supervisord 'port=127.0.0.1:9001' + serverurl rewrite to http://127.0.0.1:9001, curl checks 401/200/302/401. Confirms prior-1 supervisord/port claims.\",\"Inspected termux-boot-homelab.sh: sshd + tmux new -d -s homelab 'proot-distro login ubuntu -- supervisord -n' + 300s watchdog on :8080==401 else restart. Inspected termux-bootstrap.sh: pkg openssh/proot-distro/termux-api only; tmux+curl installed ONLY inside proot (apt), not Termux-side -- boot script needs Termux-side tmux and curl: GAP, needs 'pkg install tmux curl' or proof they exist.\",\"Contradiction: RAM is 7.4G in LINUX-SERVER.md vs 6GB RAM (Dimensity 1080 MT6877) in PORTING-NOTES.md -- memory-pressure sizing for ~213MB muse binary rests on disputed base.\",\"Web-search corroboration (10 hits, multi-source not single-source): install one-liner curl -fsSL https://dev.meta.ai/install.sh | bash, ~/.local/bin/muse launcher, Linux x86_64+arm64 incl. Ubuntu, needs only bash+curl; auth META_API