ot/Doze same as existing stack (Termux:Boot tmux + watchdog covers it). Cost: must build auth/session/agent-bridge yourself; keep filebrowser archived-binary risk in mind (upstream archived 2026-09-01, no fixes; Quantum/copyparty are maintained successors).\",\"Option3 SSH+tmux (workspace + web sources): already proven (key-only :8022, tmux installed by bootstrap, homelab already in tmux). Laptop: ssh -p 8022 over adb forward or LAN; phone-local: Termux terminal. Off-LAN: Tailscale/Headscale WireGuard mesh gives stable 100.x IPs, no port forwarding, works behind NAT/CGNAT with DERP fallback; Tailscale SSH optional. Reboot: adb forwards wiped (re-add), sshd needs Termux:Boot autostart; Doze/phantom-process killer (Android 12+) kills background sshd/services unless Termux+Boot exempted (Unrestricted), wake-lock, charger; vendor autostart toggles per dontkillmyapp. Blink/mosh notes: Blink is iOS-only so irrelevant to A34+laptop; mosh needs UDP and is optional.\"],\"notes\":[{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"Recommendation: Telegram long-polling bot for off-LAN async control (zero inbound, keeps no-public-internet posture) + keep Caddy basic-auth web UI for LAN-rich sessions + SSH+tmux over Tailscale for full terminal; all three share the existing Termux:Boot tmux + watchdog persistence. Never expose :8022/:8080/:8081 directly; rotate the admin password noted OPEN in LINUX-SERVER.md.\"}],\"unresolved\":[\"No inspected evidence of outbound internet reachability from the phone (api.telegram.org, Tailscale DERP) — assumed available; verify with curl from Termux/proot before committing to Telegram or Tailscale.\",\"Whether owner will install Tailscale app/Headscale vs staying LAN+adb-only — decision needed; no-public-internet posture favors Tailscale tailnet over any port-forward.\",\"Exact agent runtime on phone (part a, out of scope) not inspected — chat-channel choice only defines transport; the agent-to-chat bridge process still needs specifying.\"]},{\"scope\":\"critic\",\"ref\":\"prior result 3\",\"complete\":false,\"evidence\":[\"Inspected LINUX-SERVER.md: SM-A346B arm64, 7.4G RAM, Ubuntu 26.04 proot, no systemd/Docker, supervisord->Caddy :8080->filebrowser :8081 + :9001, foreground -n in tmux homelab + 300s watchdog, phone-side curl -o error 23 -> adb-push binaries, daemonized supervisord SIGKILLed screen-off, Termux:Boot proven after reboot, OPEN admin-password rotation, filebrowser v2 archived 2026-09-01.\",\"Inspected homelab-install.sh: guards ~/caddy.tgz ~/fb.tgz adb-push, Caddyfile :8080 basic_auth + /supervisor/* -> :9001 + /* -> :8081 with admin off/auto_https off, supervisord 'port=127.0.0.1:9001' + serverurl rewrite to http://127.0.0.1:9001, curl checks 401/200/302/401. Confirms prior-1 supervisord/port claims.\",\"Inspected termux-boot-homelab.sh: sshd + tmux new -d -s homelab 'proot-distro login ubuntu -- supervisord -n' + 300s watchdog on :8080==401 else restart. Inspected termux-bootstrap.sh: pkg openssh/proot-distro/termux-api only; tmux+curl installed ONLY inside proot (apt), not Termux-side -- boot script needs Termux-side tmux and curl: GAP, needs 'pkg install tmux curl' or proof they exist.\",\"Contradiction: RAM is 7.4G in LINUX-SERVER.md vs 6GB RAM (Dimensity 1080 MT6877) in PORTING-NOTES.md -- memory-pressure sizing for ~213MB muse binary rests on disputed base.\",\"Web-search corroboration (10 hits, multi-source not single-source): install one-liner curl -fsSL https://dev.meta.ai/install.sh | bash, ~/.local/bin/muse launcher, Linux x86_64+arm64 incl. Ubuntu, needs only bash+curl; auth META_API_KEY env wins > stored key > browser session, muse auth set --api-key-stdin, keys LLM_-prefixed, device/browser OAuth over SSH. Downgrades 'single-source' risk for install/auth commands.\",\"Remaining unverified: muse launcher platform-detect + exec under proot on this phone untested (same curl -o/download class failure documented); exact on-disk token path + refresh expiry uninspected