shipped 0.1.0-R708.1 binary) states 'stored at ~/.config/muse/auth.json (or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/muse/auth.json). It is not ~/.muse/'; docs.rs muse_codes::auth documents 'saved credential at ~/.config/muse/auth.json honoring XDG_CONFIG_HOME' with MUSE_AUTH_PATH-adjacent credentials_path override; multiple independent GitHub docs (quotakit, codexbar, superqode, anvil, meterbar) converge on same path + MUSE_AUTH_PATH override. macOS differs: token in login Keychain (service ai.meta.dev.credentials, account meta), auth.json only a pointer/fallback -- so on the Ubuntu-proot phone the file path above applies.","Precedence + management (official docs inspected): dev.meta.ai/docs/muse-code/auth fetched in full -- 'Muse Code uses META_API_KEY if set, then a stored key, and only then a stored browser session'; muse logout clears stored browser session + stored key but does NOT unset exported META_API_KEY; /login reopens options; MMA accounts must use API key. Matches codersera 'META_API_KEY always takes priority' line.","Practical implication for phone: device-flow login writes the file once (outbound HTTPS only); API-key route via `printf '%s' $META_API_KEY | muse auth set --api-key-stdin` lands in the same auth.json; unattended runs should prefer META_API_KEY env so expiry/logout of browser session cannot break them."],"unresolved":["Refresh-token/session expiry for muse browser login: no published value found. Official auth page (fetched full text) says only 'stores the credential... resumes where you stopped' with no lifetime/refresh numbers; targeted search for muse refresh/access-token lifetime returned only unrelated CLIs (light-oauth, rearm, grounds). Return unchanged: needs muse login --help on-device or an official lifetime statement; do not assume 30/60/90-day values from other vendors."]},"summary":"structured result submitted"},"revision":5,"role":"workflow-agent","status":"inProgress","subagentId":"01a1b7c7-13e6-7f90-a74d-ff7246dbbafd","turnId":"01a1b7c5-a944-7f03-