ibc arm64 requirement in principle; proot syscall/ptrace overhead ~40-50% UNIXbench penalty, worst for syscall/IO-heavy work (sources: kern runtime-exec research, ggprompts/termux guide via search). Caveat: proot mishandles getifaddrs()/os.networkInterfaces for Node apps and phone-side curl -o fails (workspace doc) -- same class of risk applies to the muse self-updating launcher until tested on-device.\"},{\"source\":\"primary-0\",\"ref\":\"prior result 2\",\"value\":\"Auth headless: muse login is OAuth2 device-code flow (prints code + verification URL, approve in browser) and works fine over SSH with no local browser; non-interactive/CI route is a Model API key via META_API_KEY env or muse auth set --api-key-stdin; credentials cache locally so no re-auth per session; META_API_KEY wins over logged-in session (sources: codersera guide, musecodes.io docs, qainsights, aq.dev VPS guide via search/fetch). Implication: do the device-flow login once over SSH (phone needs outbound HTTPS only), or drop an API key for unattended runs; sharing one personal login across laptop+phone concurrency/expiry not verified -- in unresolved.\"},{\"source\":\"primary-0\",\"ref\":\"prior result 2\",\"value\":\"Feasibility/mitigation reusing existing setup: run muse/muse exec inside proot Ubuntu under the existing tmux+supervisord pattern (new supervisor program or second tmux session), keep Termux battery-whitelist + Termux:Boot + watchdog; expect ~200+MB binary + model-context RAM pressure on 6-7.4GB device -- keep sessions headless (muse exec), one at a time; updater hourly self-update can be pinned with MUSE_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1; filebrowser-archived warning in workspace doc irrelevant to this task.\"},{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"Workspace LINUX-SERVER.md inspected: A34 arm64/Android16, Termux F-Droid + proot Ubuntu 26.04 (no systemd/Docker), sshd:8022 key-only, supervisord->Caddy:8080 basic-auth front + filebrowser:8081 + supervisor UI:9001; adb forward