y for muse login (only summarized as 'credentials cache locally' -- underlying file not inspected; needs muse login --help / docs page on dev.meta.ai).\",\"ref\":\"prior result 4\",\"value\":\"Practical implication for phone: device-flow login writes the file once (outbound HTTPS only); API-key route via `printf '%s' $META_API_KEY | muse auth set --api-key-stdin` lands in the same auth.json; unattended runs should prefer META_API_KEY env so expiry/logout of browser session cannot break them.\"}],\"refs\":[\"prior result 2\",\"prior result 1\",\"prior result 3\",\"prior result 4\"],\"unresolved\":[\"Whether one Meta login can be concurrently active on laptop + phone, or forces logout/session conflict (no inspected evidence).\",\"On-device proof: muse installer launcher platform-detection + binary execution under proot on this specific phone untested (proot getifaddrs/curl -o class issues suggest testing download + first run on-device before relying on it).\",\"No inspected evidence of outbound internet reachability from the phone (api.telegram.org, Tailscale DERP) — assumed available; verify with curl from Termux/proot before committing to Telegram or Tailscale.\",\"Whether owner will install Tailscale app/Headscale vs staying LAN+adb-only — decision needed; no-public-internet posture favors Tailscale tailnet over any port-forward.\",\"Exact agent runtime on phone (part a, out of scope) not inspected — chat-channel choice only defines transport; the agent-to-chat bridge process still needs specifying.\",\"Termux-side tmux+curl provenance: bootstrap does not pkg-install them; verify on-device or amend bootstrap.\",\"RAM contradiction 6GB vs 7.4G: resolve before sizing muse sessions.\",\"On-device proof: muse installer download + first run under proot; phone outbound HTTPS (dev.meta.ai, api.telegram.org, Tailscale DERP).\",\"Exact muse credential path/expiry and concurrent-login behavior.\",\"Owner decision: Tailscale vs LAN+adb-only; admin password rotation still OPEN.\",\"Refresh-token/session expiry for muse browser login: no published value found. Official auth page (fetched full text) says only 'stores the credential... resumes where you stopped' with no lifetime/refresh numbers; targeted search for muse refresh/access-token lifetime returned only unrelated CLIs (light-oauth, rearm, grounds). Return unchanged: needs muse login --help on-device or an official lifetime statement; do not assume 30/60/90-day values from other vendors.\"],\"notes\":[{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"Recommendation: Telegram long-polling bot for off-LAN async control (zero inbound, keeps no-public-internet posture) + keep Caddy basic-auth web UI for LAN-rich sessions + SSH+tmux over Tailscale for full terminal; all three share the existing Termux:Boot tmux + watchdog persistence. Never expose :8022/:8080/:8081 directly; rotate the admin password noted OPEN in LINUX-SERVER.md.\"}]}\nPrior result index:\nRead the complete prior result index with read_file using {\"path\":\"\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\danie\\\\.local\\\\share\\\\muse\\\\sessions\\\\2026\\\\11\\\\07\\\\01a1b712-7955-7a03-a1d7-21c1c82d4320\\\\tool-outputs\\\\workflow-results\\\\handoff-340740c295f66d5e818fa6eb89153ce7ca514d9d9435eccbb9ccfab96ebcb658-5cf10a2721ba26469fca495c667f9793bb6699ecb32cecb44653454105d7c1d9.txt\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":500}; keep limit at 500 and increment offset by 500 while the output says \"(more lines below)\". If a part cannot be read, name that gap and use the other readable evidence.","itemId":"eaafafe3-6167-5945-8c6a-d24f2b79204f","kind":"subagent","objective":"Workflow result handoff sha256:e1e1de8cd971e7633ec31b9d6111342a515a5a699a322b1d0580d02ac282f3e3\nCaller input bytes=13823:\nSynthesize ONLY this compact evidence into a decision-ready report for the owner (recommended harness setup + recommended comms channel with concrete next steps, plus open risks): {\"evidence\":[{\"source\":\"primary-0\",\"ref\":\"prior result 2\",\"value\":\"Workspace LINUX-SERVER.md inspected: A34 SM-A346B arm64, 7.4G RAM, Ubuntu 26.04 via proot-distro, no systemd/no Docker, supervisord->Caddy :8080->filebrowser :8081 + supervisor UI :9001, tmux session homelab + 5-min curl watchdog, Termux:Boot autostart proven after reboot, phone-side curl -o broken under proot so binaries adb-pushed from laptop, daemonized supervisord SIGKILLED under screen-off (foreground -n in tmux survives).\"},{\"source\":\"primary-0\",\"ref\":\"prior result 2\",\"value\":\"Install: muse CLI is statically linked, needs only curl+mktemp+bash, no Node/Python; Linux x86_64+arm64 supported incl. Ubuntu 20.04+; one-liner curl -fsSL https://dev.meta.ai/install.sh | bash; launcher at ~/.local/bin/muse + muse-bin-<version>; Linux arm64 binary ~213 MiB (sources: codersera install guide, backgrind, jacar.es, toolian docs via web search). Ubuntu 26.04 arm64 under proot satisfies glibc arm64 requirement in principle; proot syscall/ptrace overhead ~40-50% UNIXbench penalty, worst for syscall/IO-heavy work (sources: kern runtime-exec research, ggprompts/termux guide via search). Caveat: proot mishandles getifaddrs()/os.networkInterfaces for Node apps and phone-side curl -o fails (workspace doc) -- same class of risk applies to the muse self-updating launcher until tested on-device.\"},{\"source\":\"primary-0\",\"ref\":\"prior result 2\",\"value\":\"Auth headless: muse login is OAuth2 device-code flow (prints code + verification URL, approve in browser) and works fine over SSH with no local browser; non-interactive/CI route is a Model API key via META_API_KEY env or muse auth set --api-key-stdin; credentials cache locally so no re-auth per session; META_API_KEY wins over logged-in session (sources: codersera guide, musecodes.io docs, qainsights, aq.dev VPS guide via search/fetch). Implication: do the device-flow login once over SSH (phone needs outbound HTTPS only), or drop an API key for unattended runs; sharing one personal login across laptop+phone concurrency/expiry not verified -- in unresolved.\"},{\"source\":\"primary-0\",\"ref\":\"prior result 2\",\"value\":\"Feasibility/mitigation reusing existing setup: run muse/muse exec inside proot Ubuntu under the existing tmux+supervisord pattern (new supervisor program or second tmux session), keep Termux battery-whitelist + Termux:Boot + watchdog; expect ~200+MB binary + model-context RAM pressure on 6-7.4GB device -- keep sessions headless (muse exec), one at a time; updater hourly self-update can be pinned with MUSE_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1; filebrowser-archived warning in workspace doc irrelevant to this task.\"},{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"Workspace LINUX-SERVER.md inspected: A34 arm64/Android16, Termux F-Droid + proot Ubuntu 26.04 (no systemd/Docker), sshd:8022 key-only, supervisord->Caddy:8080 basic-auth front + filebrowser:8081 + supervisor UI:9001; adb forwards wiped on reboot, sshd does not autostart without Termux:Boot; daemonized supervisord SIGKILLed under screen-off -> runs foreground -n in tmux 'homelab' via ~/.termux/boot/homelab.sh + 5-min curl watchdog; battery whitelist + never-sleeping apps + charger required; filebrowser v2 archived 2026-09-01 keep only behind Caddy auth.\"},{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"homelab-install.sh inspected: Caddy arm64 tgz + filebrowser arm64 tgz adb-pushed (phone-side curl -o broken, error 23); Caddyfile :8080 basic_auth + reverse_proxy to :8081 and :9001, auto_https/admin off; supervisord uses 'port=127.0.0.1:9001' (http_port invalid) with supervisorctl serverurl http://127.0.0.1:9001 (unix socket missing under proot).\"},{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"termux-boot-homelab.sh inspected: boot script runs sshd + tmux new -d -s homelab 'proot-distro login ubuntu -- supervisord -n' + background 300s watchdog restarting session unless :8080 returns 401.\"},{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"termux-bootstrap.sh inspected: pkg openssh/proot-distro/termux-api, passwd+sshd, proot Ubuntu + tmux; hardening note in LINUX-SERVER.md: do NOT expose SSH directly, use Tailscale/WireGuard; keep adb authorized to laptop only.\"},{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"Option1 Telegram bot (web sources 2026): BotFather token; getUpdates long-polling = outbound HTTPS only, no public IP/ports/certs, works behind NAT/firewall; single consumer per token; polling and webhook mutually exclusive; webhook would need ports 443/80/88/8443+TLS (not usable here). Fit: best off-LAN channel preserving no-public-internet posture; runs as python script under proot/tmux or supervisord; secret = bot token + allowlist chat-id; risk: depends on api.telegram.org reachability + token hygiene; Doze/phantom-killer applies equally (needs whitelist/wakelock/boot like other services).\"},{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"Option2 custom web chat via Caddy (web sources): Caddy reverse_proxy passes Upgrade/websocket with no extra directives and streams SSE; single static arm64 binary (already proven pattern in repo). Fit: runs where filebrowser runs (extra supervisord program, e.g. :8082, Caddy handle /chat/* + basic_auth or token); reachable on LAN via adb forward tcp:8080 or phone LAN IP:8080; off-LAN only via Tailscale/tunnel, never port-forward; reboot/Doze same as existing stack (Termux:Boot tmux + watchdog covers it). Cost: must build auth/session/agent-bridge yourself; keep filebrowser archived-binary risk in mind (upstream archived 2026-09-01, no fixes; Quantum/copyparty are maintained successors).\"},{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"Option3 SSH+tmux (workspace + web sources): already proven (key-only :8022, tmux installed by bootstrap, homelab already in tmux). Laptop: ssh -p 8022 over adb forward or LAN; phone-local: Termux terminal. Off-LAN: Tailscale/Headscale WireGuard mesh gives stable 100.x IPs, no port forwarding, works behind NAT/CGNAT with DERP fallback; Tailscale SSH optional. Reboot: adb forwards wiped (re-add), sshd needs Termux:Boot autostart; Doze/phantom-process killer (Android 12+) kills background sshd/services unless Termux+Boot exempted (Unrestricted), wake-lock, charger; vendor autostart toggles per dontkillmyapp. Blink/mosh notes: Blink is iOS-only so irrelevant to A34+laptop; mosh needs UDP and is optional.\"},{\"source\":\"critic\",\"ref\":\"prior result 3\",\"value\":\"Inspected LINUX-SERVER.md: SM-A346B arm64, 7.4G RAM, Ubuntu 26.04 proot, no systemd/Docker, supervisord->Caddy :8080->filebrowser :8081 + :9001, foreground -n in tmux homelab + 300s watchdog, phone-side curl -o error 23 -> adb-push binaries, daemonized supervisord SIGKILLed screen-off, Termux:Boot proven after reboot, OPEN admin-password rotation, filebrowser v2 archived 2026-09-01.\"},{\"source\":\"critic\",\"ref\":\"prior result 3\",\"value\":\"Inspected homelab-install.sh: guards ~/caddy.tgz ~/fb.tgz adb-push, Caddyfile :8080 basic_auth + /supervisor/* -> :9001 + /* -> :8081 with admin off/auto_https off, supervisord 'port=127.0.0.1:9001' + serverurl rewrite to http://127.0.0.1:9001, curl checks 401/200/302/401. Confirms prior-1 supervisord/port claims.\"},{\"source\":\"critic\",\"ref\":\"prior result 3\",\"value\":\"Inspected termux-boot-homelab.sh: sshd + tmux new -d -s homelab 'proot-distro login ubuntu -- supervisord -n' + 300s watchdog on :8080==401 else restart. Inspected termux-bootstrap.sh: pkg openssh/proot-distro/termux-api only; tmux+curl installed ONLY inside proot (apt), not Termux-side -- boot script needs Termux-side tmux and curl: GAP, needs 'pkg install tmux curl' or proof they exist.\"},{\"source\":\"critic\",\"ref\":\"prior result 3\",\"value\":\"Contradiction: RAM is 7.4G in LINUX-SERVER.md vs 6GB RAM (Dimensity 1080 MT6877) in PORTING-NOTES.md -- memory-pressure sizing for ~213MB muse binary rests on disputed base.\"},{\"source\":\"critic\",\"ref\":\"prior result 3\",\"value\":\"Web-search corroboration (10 hits, multi-source not single-source): install one-liner curl -fsSL https://dev.meta.ai/install.sh | bash, ~/.local/bin/muse launcher, Linux x86_64+arm64 incl. Ubuntu, needs only bash+curl; auth META_API_KEY env wins > stored key > browser session, muse auth set --api-key-stdin, keys LLM_-prefixed, device/browser OAuth over SSH. Downgrades 'single-source' risk for install/auth commands.\"},{\"source\":\"critic\",\"ref\":\"prior result 3\",\"value\":\"Remaining unverified: muse launcher platform-detect + exec under proot on this phone untested (same curl -o/download class failure documented); exact on-disk token path + refresh expiry uninspected; concurrent laptop+phone single-login conflict untested; phone outbound reachability to api.telegram.org / Tailscale DERP / dev.meta.ai never curled from Termux/proot; Caddy websocket/SSE passthrough and /chat route not in repo Caddyfile (unbuilt); watchdog Termux-localhost vs proot-localhost equivalence assumed from passing curls but fragile.\"},{\"source\":\"Exact on-disk token/keychain path and refresh-token expiry for muse login (only summarized as 'credentials cache locally' -- underlying file not inspected; needs muse login --help / docs page on dev.meta.ai).\",\"ref\":\"prior result 4\",\"value\":\"On-disk credential path RESOLVED (fresh inspection): Linux/WSL/proot file is ~/.config/muse/auth.json, or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/muse/auth.json when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is set. Inspected bodies: codersera 2026 setup guide (verified against shipped 0.1.0-R708.1 binary) states 'stored at ~/.config/muse/auth.json (or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/muse/auth.json). It is not ~/.muse/'; docs.rs muse_codes::auth documents 'saved credential at ~/.config/muse/auth.json honoring XDG_CONFIG_HOME' with MUSE_AUTH_PATH-adjacent credentials_path override; multiple independent GitHub docs (quotakit, codexbar, superqode, anvil, meterbar) converge on same path + MUSE_AUTH_PATH override. macOS differs: token in login Keychain (service ai.meta.dev.credentials, account meta), auth.json only a pointer/fallback -- so on the Ubuntu-proot phone the file path above applies.\"},{\"source\":\"Exact on-disk token/keychain path and refresh-token expiry for muse login (only summarized as 'credentials cache locally' -- underlying file not inspected; needs muse login --help / docs page on dev.meta.ai).\",\"ref\":\"prior result 4\",\"value\":\"Precedence + management (official docs inspected): dev.meta.ai/docs/muse-code/auth fetched in full -- 'Muse Code uses META_API_KEY if set, then a stored key, and only then a stored browser session'; muse logout clears stored browser session + stored key but does NOT unset exported META_API_KEY; /login reopens options; MMA accounts must use API key. Matches codersera 'META_API_KEY always takes priority' line.\"},{\"source\":\"Exact on-disk token/keychain path and refresh-token expiry for muse login (only summarized as 'credentials cache locally' -- underlying file not inspected; needs muse login --help / docs page on dev.meta.ai).\",\"ref\":\"prior result 4\",\"value\":\"Practical implication for phone: device-flow login writes the file once (outbound HTTPS only); API-key route via `printf '%s' $META_API_KEY | muse auth set --api-key-stdin` lands in the same auth.json; unattended runs should prefer META_API_KEY env so expiry/logout of browser session cannot break them.\"}],\"refs\":[\"prior result 2\",\"prior result 1\",\"prior result 3\",\"prior result 4\"],\"unresolved\":[\"Whether one Meta login can be concurrently active on laptop + phone, or forces logout/session conflict (no inspected evidence).\",\"On-device proof: muse installer launcher platform-detection + binary execution under proot on this specific phone untested (proot getifaddrs/curl -o class issues suggest testing download + first run on-device before relying on it).\",\"No inspected evidence of outbound internet reachability from the phone (api.telegram.org, Tailscale DERP) — assumed available; verify with curl from Termux/proot before committing to Telegram or Tailscale.\",\"Whether owner will install Tailscale app/Headscale vs staying LAN+adb-only — decision needed; no-public-internet posture favors Tailscale tailnet over any port-forward.\",\"Exact agent runtime on phone (part a, out of scope) not inspected — chat-channel choice only defines transport; the agent-to-chat bridge process still needs specifying.\",\"Termux-side tmux+curl provenance: bootstrap does not pkg-install them; verify on-device or amend bootstrap.\",\"RAM contradiction 6GB vs 7.4G: resolve before sizing muse sessions.\",\"On-device proof: muse installer download + first run under proot; phone outbound HTTPS (dev.meta.ai, api.telegram.org, Tailscale DERP).\",\"Exact muse credential path/expiry and concurrent-login behavior.\",\"Owner decision: Tailscale vs LAN+adb-only; admin password rotation still OPEN.\",\"Refresh-token/session expiry for muse browser login: no published value found. Official auth page (fetched full text) says only 'stores the credential... resumes where you stopped' with no lifetime/refresh numbers; targeted search for muse refresh/access-token lifetime returned only unrelated CLIs (light-oauth, rearm, grounds). Return unchanged: needs muse login --help on-device or an official lifetime statement; do not assume 30/60/90-day values from other vendors.\"],\"notes\":[{\"source\":\"primary-1\",\"ref\":\"prior result 1\",\"value\":\"Recommendation: Telegram long-polling bot for off-LAN async control (zero inbound, keeps no-public-internet posture) + keep Caddy basic-auth web UI for LAN-rich sessions + SSH+tmux over Tailscale for full terminal; all three share the existing Termux:Boot tmux + watchdog persistence. Never expose :8022/:8080/:8081 directly; rotate the admin password noted OPEN in LINUX-SERVER.md.\"}]}\nPrior result index:\nRead the complete prior result index with read_file using {\"path\":\"\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\danie\\\\.local\\\\share\\\\muse\\\\sessions\\\\2026\\\\11\\\\07\\\\01a1b712-7955-7a03-a1d7-21c1c82d4320\\\\tool-outputs\\\\workflow-results\\\\handoff-340740c295f66d5e818fa6eb89153ce7ca514d9d9435eccbb9ccfab96ebcb658-5cf10a2721ba26469fca495c667f9793bb6699ecb32cecb44653454105d7c1d9.txt\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":500}; keep limit at 500 and increment offset by 500 while the output says \"(more lines below)\". If a part cannot be read, name that gap and use the other readable evidence.","recordedAt":"2026-11-07T20:51:24.037737Z","result":{"artifactRefs":[],"evidenceRefs":["run://2ad9ba50-be9a-7661-819b-d8425c44c4b5","\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\.local\\share\\muse\\sessions\\2026\\11\\07\\01a1b712-7955-7a03-a1d7-21c1c82d4320\\session.jsonl"],"structuredData":{"complete":true,"evidence":["Harness: A34 SM-A346B arm64, Ubuntu 26.04 proot (no systemd/Docker), supervisord -n in tmux 'homelab' via Termux:Boot + 300s curl watchdog on :8080==401; Caddy :8080 basic-auth -> filebrowser :8081 + supervisor :9001. Run muse/muse exec headless inside proot under same pattern (new supervisor program or 2nd tmux session), one session at a time, MUSE_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1 to pin hourly updater; ~213MiB arm64 binary + context RAM pressure is the sizing constraint.","Auth (resolved): Linux/proot credential file ~/.config/muse/auth.json (or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/muse/auth.json); macOS Keychain path does not apply. Precedence META_API_KEY env > stored key > stored browser session; `muse logout` does not unset exported META_API_KEY. Install one-liner curl -fsSL https://dev.meta.ai/install.sh | bash (needs bash+curl only), launcher ~/.local/bin/muse. Headless: device-code OAuth over SSH (outbound HTTPS only) once, or preferably META_API_KEY via `printf '%s' $META_API_KEY | muse auth set --api-key-stdin` for unattended runs.","Comms recommendation: Telegram getUpdates long-polling bot for off-LAN async control (outbound HTTPS only, no inbound ports, keeps no-public-internet posture; BotFather token + chat-id allowlist; runs under proot/tmux or supervisord) + keep Caddy basic-auth web UI for LAN-rich sessions (add :8082 + /chat/* route; Caddy passes Upgrade/websocket and SSE with no extra directives) + SSH+tmux key-only :8022 over adb/LAN now, Tailscale tailnet for off-LAN terminal (no port-forward, DERP fallback). Never expose :8022/:8080/:8081 directly.","Next steps: 1) On-device: pkg install tmux curl (Termux-side gap) and verify; 2) curl from Termux+proot: dev.meta.ai, api.telegram.org, Tailscale DERP; 3) adb-push or ~/caddy.tgz-pattern install muse, run first `muse exec` under proot; 4) device-flow login once over SSH or set META_API_KEY; 5) BotFather token + allowlist bot script under supervisord/tmux; 6) add Caddy /chat route + :8082 service; 7) install Tailscale app, rotate OPEN admin password, confirm Termux:Boot + whitelist + charger + watchdog survive reboot/screen-off."],"unresolved":["On-device proof: muse download + first run under proot; phone outbound HTTPS (dev.meta.ai, api.telegram.org, Tailscale DERP).","muse browser-session refresh/access-token lifetime: no published value; needs on-device `muse login --help` or official statement.","Concurrent laptop+phone single-login conflict untested.","Termux-side tmux+curl provenance gap; RAM 6GB vs 7.4G contradiction.","Owner decisions: Tailscale vs LAN+adb-only; admin password rotation OPEN; agent-to-chat bridge unspecified."]},"summary":"structured result submitted"},"revision":5,"role":"workflow-agent","status":"inProgress","subagentId":"01a1b7c7-9727-75e2-a51f-76fab65848e7","turnId":"01a1b7c5-a944-7f03-b294-f5c3e0964d0e","usage":{"cacheReadTokens":26737,"cacheWriteTokens":0,"cachedTokens":26737,"inputTokens":58514,"outputTokens":1299,"reasoningTokens":92},"workflowRunId":"workflow-run-model-tool-call_01a1b7c610df7134a294d7c0e84a6431"},"opened_ordinal":1604,"span":{"first":{"id":"01a1b712-7955-787f-85d8-2a82a5e924b5","sequence":8774},"last":{"id":"01a1b7c7-c105-7f22-9cf2-575b65ecceb3","sequence":8788},"stream_id":"01a1b712-7